        <briefdescription>
<para>Returns the singleton for T, constructing it on first use. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The fast path looks up the type under the mutex and returns the existing instance. On a miss the object is constructed outside the lock (see the inline comment below) and then re-checked under the lock before being published, so concurrent first calls cannot install two different instances. Constructor arguments are therefore only used on the first successful construction and ignored on later calls. <parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Type to look up or create; its type_index is the inventory key. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Args</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Constructor argument types for T. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">args</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Arguments forwarded to T&apos;s constructor when a new object is needed. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>A shared_ptr to the registered singleton; ownership is shared with all other callers and with the <ref refid="classStore" kindref="compound">Store</ref>. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>Marked nodiscard because callers are expected to use the shared instance; the <ref refid="classStore" kindref="compound">Store</ref> itself retains a strong reference in the inventory. (&quot;Strong reference&quot; means a shared_ptr that keeps the object alive.) </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classStore_1a1e12f060c02095975351db8f5d63cb76" kindref="member">registerObject()</ref>, <ref refid="classStore_1aaf81da54b109478891030b7e04653bad" kindref="member">cachedObject()</ref>, <ref refid="classStore_1a2a4bfc0b18f2999216eda3067988cf57" kindref="member">replaceObject()</ref> </para>
